# Controls what `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the build context.
#
# `.dockerignore` does NOT apply here — gcloud reads this file, and without it
# falls back to deriving rules from .gitignore, which is close but not guaranteed.
# Being explicit keeps the upload to a few MB of source instead of a 600 MB
# node_modules tree if someone has run `npm install` locally first.
#
# Everything excluded here is either regenerated inside the image (node_modules
# via `npm ci`, fixtures via `npm run seed`, dist via tsc) or irrelevant to a build.

.git
.gitignore
.github

node_modules
**/node_modules

.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo
out
**/out

# Regenerated in the image by `npm run seed` — 47 MB that must not be uploaded.
apps/api/data

coverage
test-results
playwright-report

# MUST stay anchored with a leading slash. These patterns use gitignore
# semantics, so a bare `perf` matches *any* directory of that name — including
# apps/web/src/app/perf, the /perf route. That excluded the route from the build
# context and the deployed site returned 404 for it while working locally.
/perf/

*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.local
**/.env
**/.env.local
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Docs and local-only tooling. package-lock.json is deliberately NOT excluded —
# `npm ci` in the Dockerfile requires it.
*.md
**/*.md
